    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA rare opportunity to acquire a derelict residence with a range of adjoining outbuildings in one of North County Dublin's most desirable coastal settings.\n\nHaving been vacant for an extended period, the property may qualify for assistance under the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant and the Derelict Property Top-Up Grant, subject to purchasers satisfying the relevant eligibility criteria and approval by Fingal County Council.\n\nIdeally positioned on Channel Road, just minutes from Rush Golf Club and the beach, Rush is a vibrant and well-established coastal town offering an excellent range of amenities. Residents enjoy convenient access to shops, cafés, restaurants, traditional pubs, schools, sporting facilities and the local theatre, together with miles of coastline and a wide variety of beach and water-based recreational activities.\n\nRush/Lusk Train Station is only a five-minute drive away, while the M1 motorway can be reached in approximately 15 minutes. The M50, Dublin Airport, and Swords are all within a 2025-minute drive. Rush also benefits from an excellent bus service to Dublin city centre."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
